00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.462
Jennifer Check was most likely born in 1992.

00:00:02.516 --> 00:00:05.438
I noticed the movie theater marquee in her town is showing Baby Mama and

00:00:05.444 --> 00:00:08.398
Forgetting Sarah Marshall, both of which came out in April 2008,

00:00:08.404 --> 00:00:10.382
and the script states that Jennifer is 16 years old.

00:00:10.436 --> 00:00:14.151
Jennifer grew up in a small town of just 7000 known as Devil's Kettle, Minnesota, 

00:00:14.151 --> 00:00:17.146
where she met her lifelong best friend, Anita Lesnicki,

00:00:17.178 --> 00:00:19.797
who became known as Needy for short due to her attachment to her

00:00:19.797 --> 00:00:21.198
more popular and outgoing friend.

00:00:21.284 --> 00:00:24.254
From the very beginning, Jennifer is in charge of the relationship,

00:00:24.292 --> 00:00:27.493
getting the better barbies in the sandbox as kids, stealing Anita's toys,

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:31.814
pouring lemonade on Anita's bed, mocking her for being scared of a boombox at Girl Scout camp,

00:00:31.814 --> 00:00:33.526
and eventually calling all the shots in the friendship as teenagers. 

00:00:33.548 --> 00:00:37.910
Still, they remain attached as evidenced by their matching BFF necklaces.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:39.370
-[Anita] That's why we're biffs.

00:00:40.201 --> 00:00:42.838
Though Needy's feelings for Jennifer seem to go beyond that.

00:00:43.151 --> 00:00:47.062
At one point they got blitzed on Peach Schnapps and Jennifer became her first kiss.

00:00:47.126 --> 00:00:49.754
She claims that they're not lipstick lesbos as she puts it.

00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:52.602
In Jennifer's case, she seems to be bisexual, but she leans more towards

00:00:52.656 --> 00:00:53.690
being interested in men.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.846
While Jennifer was always a cruel friend, the onset of puberty really seems

00:00:56.868 --> 00:01:00.158
to magnify her behavior, and although Needy may not realize it yet,

00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:02.778
the reason Jennifer acts the way she does is out of insecurity.

00:01:02.874 --> 00:01:07.000
She does a number of things to cover this up, like hooking up with Eric Bogart at summer camp,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.351
losing her virginity in junior high, taking laxatives to stay skinny, 

00:01:10.351 --> 00:01:13.431
spitting a lot of profanity, and wearing a mask of insincerity 

00:01:13.431 --> 00:01:15.842
to hide the fact that she cares what people think about her.

00:01:15.896 --> 00:01:18.494
I mean, her vanity is filled with pictures of herself.

00:01:18.622 --> 00:01:21.654
It's possible that some or most of this insecurity comes from being

00:01:21.692 --> 00:01:22.770
abandoned by her father.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.478
All of the behaviors that I just listed are prime examples of what the

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:28.402
modern Internet would probably refer to as fatherless behavior.

00:01:28.466 --> 00:01:31.560
And while this is just a meme term used to stereotype people,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.710
it does come from a real place.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.986
There is actual research to suggest that teenage girls with an absent father figure

00:01:36.018 --> 00:01:38.790
are twice as likely to be promiscuous and act out.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:42.074
The idea is that girls who grew up without a father will seek male attention

00:01:42.122 --> 00:01:42.954
to fill that void.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.898
There's not a lot of focus on this, but it feels deliberate that Jennifer's

00:01:45.914 --> 00:01:48.126
father is never mentioned and her mom is single.

00:01:48.228 --> 00:01:50.151
-[Jennifer] My mom has a date with that guy who owns the ham store.

00:01:50.151 --> 00:01:52.730
In 2006, Jen was the snowflake queen.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.270
We never find out what that is.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.781
I'm assuming it's either a part in a school play or an honor given out at a

00:01:56.781 --> 00:02:00.226
winter themed school dance, but it's clear that it's yet another cover of

00:02:00.248 --> 00:02:01.406
Jennifer's insecurity.

00:02:01.518 --> 00:02:05.246
-[Jennifer] How could I ever be insecure? I was the Snowflake Queen.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:08.366
In high school, Jen became a flag twirler on color guard, where she's

00:02:08.398 --> 00:02:11.046
featured front and center in the performances, the perfect spot to get

00:02:11.068 --> 00:02:12.002
attention from boys.

00:02:12.066 --> 00:02:15.334
But at the end of the day, an insecure teenager who spends her time watching

00:02:15.372 --> 00:02:19.286
fitness videos, browsing Myspace, and listening to Fallout Boy in 2008

00:02:19.308 --> 00:02:20.482
is not that out of the ordinary.

00:02:20.546 --> 00:02:24.826
But Jennifer's ordinary life became anything but on one February evening,

00:02:24.848 --> 00:02:28.106
When an indie rock band she was fawning over tried to sacrifice her to Satan

00:02:28.128 --> 00:02:31.338
at the base of a waterfall while singing a Tommy Tutone song.

00:02:31.344 --> 00:02:34.346
To learn the meaning behind the often misunderstood oddities of Jennifer's body,

